From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 08:00:22 +0100
Subject: drm/lima: flush the L2 cache and TLB after growing the heap

On a PLBU out-of-memory interrupt, lima_sched_recover_work() flushes the
L2 cache and zaps the MMU TLB, and only then lima_gp_task_recover() grows
the heap (mapping new pages) and restarts the PLBU allocation. The Mali
MMU fetches page table entries through the L2 cache. Any table walk in
between (most likely by a PP core rendering the previous frame, which
shares the L2 and the page table lines) can leave the not yet valid
entries of the new heap pages cached, and the restarted PLBU then faults
on a page whose PTE is valid in memory:

  lima 1c40000.gpu: gpmmu page fault at 0x45c9000 from bus id 0 of type read

Here the tile heap is mapped at 0x45c1000 and has just grown from 32 KiB
to 64 KiB: the fault hits the first new page, and the PTE read by the CPU
at fault time is valid. The fault always came with the second GP job of
a new GL context, as the first PP job of that context completed.

Flush the caches after the heap has been grown, right before the PLBU
allocation is updated. ARM's Mali-400 kernel driver (r3p0,
mali_group_resume_gp_with_new_heap()) also invalidates the L2 and zaps
the TLB right before it resumes the GP with the new heap.

Tested on an Allwinner A10 (Mali-400 MP1) with a three-scene glmark2
sequence and the other patches of this series applied: with
lima.heap_init_nr_pages=1 (many heap grows per frame) the fault hit 5 of
20 runs before this change and 0 of 40 runs after it. With the default
heap size it showed up after 5 and 28 runs in two sessions before, and
0 of 80 runs after (indicative only at that rate). Also running on an
Allwinner A20 (Mali-400 MP2), where the fault is rarer.

Fixes: 2081e8dcf1ee ("drm/lima: recover task by enlarging heap buffer")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c    |  6 ++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c | 10 +++++++---
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h |  1 +
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c
@@ -264,6 +264,12 @@ static int lima_gp_task_recover(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe)
 			return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The MMU walks the page tables through the L2 cache: drop stale
+	 * entries of the new heap pages only after they have been mapped.
+	 */
+	lima_sched_pipe_flush_caches(pipe);
+
 	gp_write(LIMA_GP_INT_MASK, LIMA_GP_IRQ_MASK_USED);
 	/* Resume from where we stopped, i.e. new start is old end */
 	gp_write(LIMA_GP_PLBU_ALLOC_START_ADDR,
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.c
@@ -510,10 +510,8 @@ static const struct drm_sched_backend_ops lima_sched_ops = {
 	.free_job = lima_sched_free_job,
 };
 
-static void lima_sched_recover_work(struct work_struct *work)
+void lima_sched_pipe_flush_caches(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe)
 {
-	struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe =
-		container_of(work, struct lima_sched_pipe, recover_work);
 	int i;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < pipe->num_l2_cache; i++)
@@ -525,6 +523,12 @@ static void lima_sched_recover_work(struct work_struct *work)
 		for (i = 0; i < pipe->num_mmu; i++)
 			lima_mmu_flush_tlb(pipe->mmu[i]);
 	}
+}
+
+static void lima_sched_recover_work(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe =
+		container_of(work, struct lima_sched_pipe, recover_work);
 
 	if (pipe->task_recover(pipe))
 		drm_sched_fault(&pipe->base);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_sched.h
@@ -106,6 +106,7 @@ struct dma_fence *lima_sched_context_queue_task(struct lima_sched_task *task);
 int lima_sched_pipe_init(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe, const char *name);
 void lima_sched_pipe_fini(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe);
 void lima_sched_pipe_task_done(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe);
+void lima_sched_pipe_flush_caches(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe);
 
 static inline void lima_sched_pipe_mmu_error(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe)
 {
-- 
